# fixedbugs, defect 2372, lane b26-cli, 2026-11-09.
#
# The header makes the bound `top2372_alias` a macro for `base2372_alias`,
# so the call this program's C writes is one to `base2372_alias`, which
# nothing on the link line defines; the linker names the compiler's own
# functions as referring to it. Until 2026-11-09 it was *internal error:
# linking failed* at exit 2; the macro is now read, and told.

extern "fixedbugs-2372-alias.h"
    function top2372_alias() -> i32  #~ ffi_missing_link

function main()
    print(top2372_alias())
